  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>
  <p>
    Do not buy another certification course before you have picked your target platform and set up a free
    tier account for a real project. That single decision does more for your odds than another week of
    watching cloud fundamentals videos.
  </p>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>Pick one career path from the four above based on the daily work, not the job title.</p>
    <p>Then pick one platform based on job postings in your target city, and start a real lab project before scheduling any exam.</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    Moving toward earlier financial freedom through cloud skills works the same way it does in any
    high-value skill lane: the right platform choice, visible lab proof, and a certification that backs up
    something you can already demonstrate, stacked deliberately rather than collected at random. If you want
    a second opinion on whether cloud computing fits your specific background and city,
